      "/api/pending": {
        "get": {
          "summary": "List Pending",
          "description": "All drafts in the pending queue.\n\nEnvelope-only. The list enumerates run directories under the\nworkspace ingestion-runs root via the store. The run id IS the row\nidentity — same id the upload route allocated, same id every URL\naddresses. With one run per directory there is no cross-class\nstem collision to detect: run id uniqueness is a property of the\nstore's directory layout, so the ambiguity row is gone.\n\nListing exclusively from envelopes closes a class of bugs\nstructurally: there's only one surface to enumerate, one\nidentity rule, and no dedup logic to get wrong.",
          "operationId": "list_pending_api_pending_get",
          "responses": {
            "200": {
              "description": "Successful Response",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "items": {
                      "additionalProperties": true,
                      "type": "object"
                    },
                    "type": "array",
                    "title": "Response List Pending Api Pending Get"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "/api/pending/{draft_id}": {
        "get": {
          "summary": "Get Pending",
          "description": "Envelope-first read. The envelope IS the review surface;\n`state/pending/\u003Cid\u003E.yaml` is no longer a fallback.\n\nOutcomes:\n  - envelope exists → project from envelope, return the\n    review payload (draft, raw, workflow, etc.). `raw` is\n    generated from the envelope, not read from disk — the\n    editor renders it unchanged.\n  - no envelope → 404.\n\nPut keeps the envelope fresh on every UI edit, so an\nenvelope-source response always reflects the latest reviewer\nstate.",
          "operationId": "get_pending_api_pending__draft_id__get",
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "draft_id",
              "in": "path",
              "required": true,
              "schema": {
                "type": "string",
                "title": "Draft Id"
              }
            }
          ],
          "responses": {
            "200": {
              "description": "Successful Response",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "additionalProperties": true,
                    "title": "Response Get Pending Api Pending  Draft Id  Get"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "422": {
              "description": "Validation Error",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "put": {
          "summary": "Put Pending",
          "description": "Update the canonical `.ingest.json` envelope from a\nUI-shaped YAML payload.\n\nFlow:\n  1. Validate the UI's YAML-shaped payload through the\n     accepted-family raw boundary (RawCatalogEntryDocument). This\n     catches level violations, vocab issues, schema-unknown\n     attrs, and the retired `prefix:` / `status:` top-level\n     fields — same gate accepted YAML loading uses.\n  2. Translate the validated raw model to an ArtifactBody via\n     `yaml_dict_to_envelope_body`. The translator enforces\n     the per-fact provenance contract (snippet + page on\n     every non-literal source) so Put can't degrade\n     canonical provenance.\n  3. Load the existing envelope if any (preserves\n     `document_id`, `ingestion_run`, `annotations`,\n     `state_history`) or build a fresh envelope.\n  4. Replace `body` with the translated one; map UI\n     `review_status` onto envelope.state; append a\n     state_history entry only when state actually changes.\n  5. Run `smoke_check` in memory against the updated body.\n     Non-OK → 422 with the rendered report, no disk write.\n  6. Persist the envelope atomically through the store\n     (`create_run` for a first-time Put, `save_run` otherwise).\n     No companion YAML projection is written.\n\nOnly the `.ingest.json` envelope is written, so the prior\nYAML-replace failure modes — and the documented \"rollback only\nhandles new envelopes\" limit — don't exist here.",
          "operationId": "put_pending_api_pending__draft_id__put",
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "draft_id",
              "in": "path",
              "required": true,
              "schema": {
                "type": "string",
                "title": "Draft Id"
              }
            }
          ],
          "requestBody": {
            "required": true,
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PutBody"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "responses": {
            "200": {
              "description": "Successful Response",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "additionalProperties": {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    "title": "Response Put Pending Api Pending  Draft Id  Put"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "422": {
              "description": "Validation Error",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "/api/pending/{draft_id}/accept": {
        "post": {
          "summary": "Accept Pending",
          "description": "Stage a reviewed draft into the local product tree.\n\nLocal product-repo *staging*, not a runtime publish and not\nproduction approval. Enabled only when `PARTS_INGESTION_ENABLED` is\ntrue (local authoring); deployed mode 403s here (the API is the\nboundary, not the hidden tab). The configured workspace `product/`\ntree is the target — there is no separate product-checkout concept.\n\nOn success Accept:\n  - projects the reviewed candidate YAML from the run's envelope\n    (the single source of truth; the request body is not\n    consulted);\n  - copies the run-local `source.pdf` into the product tree at\n    `product/datasheets/\u003Cclass\u003E/\u003Cstem\u003E.pdf`;\n  - rewrites the YAML citation to the product-relative\n    `datasheets/\u003Cclass\u003E/\u003Cstem\u003E.pdf`;\n  - smoke-validates the candidate against the product schemas/vocab\n    before any write;\n  - writes `product/entries/\u003Cclass\u003E/\u003Cstem\u003E.yaml`;\n  - reloads the in-memory catalog so a local match sees it\n    immediately;\n  - deletes the run directory (envelope + source PDF) — the\n    product repo's Git history is the audit trail.\n\nIt does NOT commit, does NOT require DB credentials, and does NOT\nmean \"approved for production\". The staged YAML + PDF are left as a\nGit working-tree diff for the developer to inspect, test, commit,\nand PR — Git/PR remains the approval and deploy path.\n\nErrors:\n  - 403 — ingestion authoring disabled (deployed posture).\n  - 404 — no run at this draft_id.\n  - 409 — the source PDF is missing, or staging would clobber an\n    existing datasheet target.\n  - 422 — envelope present but body not yet projectable, missing\n    class/entry, or fails the catalog smoke gate.\n  - 500 — disk failure promoting the PDF or writing the YAML.",
          "operationId": "accept_pending_api_pending__draft_id__accept_post",
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "draft_id",
              "in": "path",
              "required": true,
              "schema": {
                "type": "string",
                "title": "Draft Id"
              }
            }
          ],
          "responses": {
            "200": {
              "description": "Successful Response",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "additionalProperties": true,
                    "title": "Response Accept Pending Api Pending  Draft Id  Accept Post"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "422": {
              "description": "Validation Error",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
